Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Cold Open as the 3rd worker product

Registers Cold Open (cold-email outbound) as a full product alongside
Showtime and Reputation Manager, following the exact same pattern those
two already established end to end:

- 7 skills (icp-lock, voice-capture, source-connect, send-connect,
  daily-send, reply-sort, send-report) via cold-open-skill-manifest.ts /
  cold-open-skill-registry.ts, wired into the existing 4-catalog Inngest
  dispatcher (src/inngest/skill.ts) and worker-registry.ts's WorkerId
  union, categories, and config-field catalog.
- coldOpenConfig/coldOpenLeads/coldOpenReplies tables (schema.ts +
  migration) mirroring the Cold Open skill pack's own coldopen.config.md
  spine, with real engagement-skills.ts evidence-based enrollment
  matching Reputation Manager's own pattern.
- Real server-side execution: ported hash-rotation, subject/body variant
  rotation + validation, a business-status liveness check, and an
  SPF/DKIM/DMARC gap checker from the Cold Open skill pack; 4 ESP
  adapters (Instantly/SmartLead/Lemlist/Reply.io) and a CSV lead
  fetcher against this app's own credential vault; a Haiku-based reply
  classifier; and a daily-send orchestrator (fetch -> historical dedupe
  -> liveness -> assemble copy -> push -> report) with a dry-run-by-
  default live-send gate, dispatched by an hourly local-time Inngest
  cron using the same enablement-gate-before-startRun pattern the rest
  of this app's crons already use.
- Bridge routes + 5 worker-config-forms components + workers-panel.tsx
  wiring so a client is enabled and configured for Cold Open the exact
  same way as any other worker (toggle -> configure inline), and a
  Library listing (WORKSPACE_PRODUCTS) so it installs and browses the
  same way Showtime/Reputation Manager already do.

Apify/Sales Navigator lead fetching beyond a config/credential check,
and SmartLead/Lemlist/Reply.io reply feeds, are explicitly flagged
unbuilt rather than faked, matching this app's own "ask, flagged
unbuilt" convention (see e.g. pre-call-read's personMatchConfidenceThreshold).

